From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: third_party: only include test-only dependencies when tests are enabled

googletest and yaml-cpp are consumed exclusively by test code:

  * googletest by umd/vpu_driver/unit_tests, by
    umd/level_zero_driver/unit_tests and by validation/test-app-lib
  * yaml-cpp by validation/umd-test

third_party/CMakeLists.txt nevertheless includes cmake/googletest.cmake
and cmake/yaml-cpp.cmake unconditionally. Both helpers try find_package()
first and then fall back to add_subdirectory() on the bundled submodule,
so a build that enables neither the validation tests nor the unit tests
still has to supply those dependencies: either by checking out submodules
whose contents it never compiles, or by installing test-only development
packages.

That is awkward for distribution packaging, where bundled copies of
third-party sources are commonly disallowed, and where the release
tarballs do not carry submodule contents in the first place.

Include the two helpers only when something in the build actually links
against them. Builds using the default options are unaffected, since
ENABLE_VALIDATION_BUILD defaults to ON.

ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS is introduced by the accompanying "umd: add
ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS" change. Should that be applied separately, CMake
evaluates the undefined variable as false, which is the intended
behaviour here.

Signed-off-by: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>

---
 third_party/CMakeLists.txt | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/third_party/CMakeLists.txt b/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
index da922e0..52f9d59 100644
--- a/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -14,6 +14,19 @@ if (ENABLE_NPU_PERFETTO_BUILD)
   include(cmake/perfetto.cmake)
 endif()
 
-include(cmake/googletest.cmake)
-include(cmake/yaml-cpp.cmake)
+# googletest and yaml-cpp are test-only dependencies: googletest is
+# consumed by umd/*/unit_tests/ (ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS) and by
+# validation/test-app-lib/, yaml-cpp only by validation/umd-test/.
+# Both helper modules fall back to add_subdirectory() on the vendored
+# third_party/googletest and third_party/yaml-cpp submodules when no
+# system package is found, so including them unconditionally makes a
+# driver-only build depend on sources it never compiles. Only pull them
+# in when something in the build actually links against them.
+if (ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS OR ENABLE_VALIDATION_BUILD)
+  include(cmake/googletest.cmake)
+endif()
+
+if (ENABLE_VALIDATION_BUILD)
+  include(cmake/yaml-cpp.cmake)
+endif()
 
